    "caveats": [
      "Verify the physiological gut-lumen shear target against primary literature for your specific gut segment (small-intestine villus tip vs. crypt vs. colon); 0.002–0.02 Pa is a defensible range but segment-specific values vary.",
      "The registry does not list a Caco-2 shear range — the 0.01 Pa target is anchored to gut-lumen physiology, not to a Caco-2-specific value.",
      "Caco-2 needs ~21 days to differentiate into a tight monolayer (TEER ≥ ~300 Ω·cm²); apply flow only after the monolayer has established, or ramp flow gradually to avoid detaching immature cells.",
      "Confirm the channel floor area (0.2 cm² assumed for 1000 µm × 20 mm) matches your actual device footprint before seeding.",
      "At 2.25 µL/min the medium turnover is slow (residence ~80 s); use a recirculating reservoir or frequent medium exchange to avoid nutrient depletion over multi-day culture."
    ]
